---
// The 2.0 subscription tiers. Built 2026-08-31; the 1.x What's New card links to
// /licensing, so this page carries the 2.0 story. Static: no accounts or checkout wired yet.
//
// TENSE IS PRESENT, AS-SHIPPED, by Adrian's order (2026-08-31): the page reads as if 2.0
// and subscriptions are live, so the deploy needs no second copy pass. No "arrives with",
// no "coming", no "opens with 2.0" anywhere in rendered text.
//
// NAMING, IN CONCRETE (Adrian, 2026-08-31): the product is the STUDIO PIPELINE, never
// "the Maya toolset" - it includes the Unreal Control Rig builder now. Product pages
// split three ways: Armature, Pipeline, Control Rig.
//
// EVERY PRICE traces to ONE file and nowhere else:
// _TheBridge/StandingOrders/Knowledge/commercial-model.md (current truth for the
// commercial model; it supersedes the seat-subscription PRICING.md and carries the
// 2026-08-31 rulings: modules in the subscription, 1.x phased out, Armature free,
// Studio Pipeline naming).
//
// THE MODEL IS FINAL (Adrian, 2026-08-31: "this should be the final pricing model").
// Every former open line is ruled in commercial-model.md:
//   - Freelance Tech Art has ONE add-on: Animation, $9/week, which makes it all tools
//     (ANIM tab, Export All Animation Clips, FS Control Rig, Ribbon Modules).
//     It is an add-on on one tier, never rendered as a fifth tier.
//   - Base Freelance Tech Art carries neither the Ribbon Modules nor FS Control Rig.
//   - Pro has a yearly price: $450, same two-months-free shape as Premium.
//   - Support: "priority" email is THE ONLY wording allowed. NEVER a response time,
//     in hours or days, anywhere on any surface.
//   - Enterprise seats carry Pro support at every band.
//   - The weekly band BILLS WEEKLY, recurring (Adrian, 2026-09-02: "Let's do weekly
//     payments for the weekly people"). It replaced the prepaid 1/4/12-week blocks; a
//     weekly seat renews itself and cancels in the same portal as every other tier.
// Refund windows are ruled but the attorney reviews wording before it reaches a page,
// so this page carries NO refund copy.
//
// Copy voice: Adrian rules every word. Drafted for his ruling, not shipped as final.
// No em-dashes anywhere in this file's rendered text.
//
// BUY BUTTONS wired 2026-09-02. Every plan id and price lives in ONE place, src/data/plans.ts
// (the single spot a real Stripe payment link URL gets pasted later); this file only reads
// it. A visitor with no fs_session in localStorage can never reach checkout directly: a
// purchase made without a signed-in account cannot be attached to a seat, so every buy
// control sends a signed-out visitor to /account/ first instead. See the client script at
// the bottom of this file for the session check and the client_reference_id / prefilled_email
// query-string handoff, both built from GET /v1/account.
import { PLANS } from '../data/plans';
const plan = (id: string) => PLANS.find((p) => p.id === id)!;


// ==========================================================================================
// REBUILT 2026-09-03 FROM ADRIAN'S DESIGN DROP.
// Source: Inbox/Website_fabricatorstudio/HTML/"Armature Pricing.html", a Claude Design
// canvas export. Read, never modified: the Inbox is his and is read-only to the crew.
//
// The drop was built against this site's OWN system - Archivo and Instrument Serif, and
// carbon / iron / bone / plasma at their exact token values - so nothing here invents a
// colour or a typeface. The single literal that is not a token is the cobalt rail #33547E,
// darker than --cobalt-dim, and it is his.
//
// WHAT THE DESIGN CHANGED, past the paint:
//   1. A BILLING SELECTOR PER CARD. Weekly / Monthly / Yearly is a segmented control, and
//      the price, the alt line and the button all follow it. It replaces a row of one
//      button per plan, which put three prices on screen at once and asked the reader to
//      pick a checkout rather than a plan.
//   2. A FEATURE GLYPH THAT MATCHES ITS SENSE. Yes is a plasma tick, no is a dim cross.
//      This is the fix for the defect he was shown the same day: the Animator card's "No
//      rigging or skinning tools" was rendering with a GREEN TICK next to it.
//   3. ONE CTA PER CARD, in its own words, with a footnote beneath.
//   4. Pro lifts 10px and wears the plasma rail, border, glow and button.
//
// ENTERPRISE SAYS "TALK TO US" AND OPENS MAIL, NOT CHECKOUT. The design says so and it
// agrees with the standing note below that Enterprise is never a buy button. Its monthly
// and yearly prices still show; the seat is arranged by conversation.
// ==========================================================================================

// The "was" figures are the design's, and each is an EQUIVALENT rather than a price anyone
// was charged: $180 is twelve months at $15, $300 is twelve at $25, $540 is twelve at $45,
// and $10 is the two freelance halves bought separately. They are struck through to show
// what the longer commitment saves.
//
// ONE OF THEM DISAGREES WITH THE COMMERCIAL MODEL AND IS FLAGGED TO HIM: the drop puts $16
// on the Animator monthly, being four weeks at $4. commercial-model.md computes that band's
// monthly equivalent as $17.33, because a month is 4.33 weeks and not 4. Rendered as the
// design has it, pending his ruling.
const TIERS = [
  {
    key: 'animator',
    name: 'Freelance animator',
    summary: 'The animation tools and the Unreal builder.',
    cta: 'Start animating',
    footnote: '',
    // `sel` is the band the card opens on; his design opens the Animator on Monthly.
    sel: 'animator_m',
    plans: [
      { id: 'animator_w', label: 'Weekly', was: '', alt: 'or $15 / month, or $150 / year', tip: 'Billed weekly, cancel any time' },
      { id: 'animator_m', label: 'Monthly', was: '$16', alt: 'or $4 / week, or $150 / year', tip: 'Billed monthly' },
      { id: 'animator_y', label: 'Yearly', was: '$180', alt: 'two months free, or $15 / month', tip: 'Billed once a year, two months free' },
    ],
    features: [
      ['yes', 'Anim Studio, and the exporter ANIM tab'],
      ['yes', 'Unreal Control Rig builder'],
      ['yes', 'Armature advanced'],
      ['no', 'No rigging or skinning tools'],
    ],
  },
  {
    key: 'techart',
    name: 'Freelance tech art',
    summary: 'The tech art tools, billed weekly.',
    cta: 'Start building',
    footnote: 'Billed weekly, cancel any time',
    sel: 'techart_w',
    plans: [
      { id: 'techart_w', label: 'Weekly', was: '', alt: 'or $9 / week with Animation: all tools', tip: 'The tech art tools alone' },
      { id: 'techart_anim_w', label: '+ Animation', was: '$10', alt: 'tech art and animation, every freelance tool', tip: 'Tech art plus the Animation add-on' },
    ],
    features: [
      ['yes', 'The tech art tools'],
      ['yes', 'Exporter: MODEL and RIG tabs'],
      ['yes', 'Billed weekly, cancel any time'],
    ],
  },
  {
    key: 'pro',
    name: 'Pro',
    featured: true,
    summary: 'Every tool in the studio.',
    cta: 'Get Pro',
    footnote: '',
    sel: 'pro_m',
    plans: [
      { id: 'pro_m', label: 'Monthly', was: '', alt: 'or $250 / year, two months free', tip: 'Billed monthly' },
      { id: 'pro_y', label: 'Yearly', was: '$300', alt: 'two months free, or $25 / month', tip: 'Billed once a year, two months free' },
    ],
    features: [
      ['yes', 'Maya rigging and animation tools'],
      ['yes', 'Unreal Control Rig builder'],
      ['yes', 'Advanced Ribbon Modules'],
      ['yes', 'Monthly or yearly'],
    ],
  },
  {
    key: 'enterprise',
    name: 'Enterprise',
    summary: 'Pro plus support.',
    cta: 'Talk to us',
    mailto: 'mailto:licensing@fabricator.studio?subject=Enterprise',
    footnote: '',
    sel: 'enterprise_m',
    plans: [
      { id: 'enterprise_m', label: 'Monthly', was: '', alt: 'or $450 / year, two months free', tip: 'Billed monthly' },
      { id: 'enterprise_y', label: 'Yearly', was: '$540', alt: 'two months free, or $45 / month', tip: 'Billed once a year, two months free' },
    ],
    features: [
      ['yes', 'Everything in Pro'],
      ['yes', 'Priority email support'],
    ],
  },
];

// Each card is RENDERED IN ITS OPENING STATE rather than assembled by script, so the page
// is correct and readable with JavaScript off, which is also what a crawler and reader mode
// receive. The script only swaps the three price fields and the button target on a press.
const view = TIERS.map((t) => {
  const open = t.plans.find((p) => p.id === t.sel) ?? t.plans[0];
  return { ...t, open, openPlan: plan(open.id) };
});
// THE PER-SEAT LADDER IS NOT RENDERED, and it is not deleted either.
//
// It was the Enterprise tier's pricing until 2026-09-02, when Adrian renamed Premium to
// Pro and Pro to Enterprise. "Enterprise" is now the $45 tier above, and Stripe carries
// four products with no fifth, so a banded per-seat table under the same word would tell
// a visitor two different prices for one name.
//
// Kept in the file, unrendered, because retiring the volume ladder is a commercial
// decision and nobody has made it out loud. Flip SHOW_SEAT_LADDER to bring it back, or
// delete both once it is ruled.
const SHOW_SEAT_LADDER = false;

// The ladder is marginal: each band prices only the seats inside it.
const BANDS = [
  { seats: '1 to 5', fee: '$50' },
  { seats: '6 to 50', fee: '$25' },
  { seats: '51 to 100', fee: '$15' },
  { seats: '101 to 200', fee: '$8' },
  { seats: '201 to 250', fee: '$4' },
  { seats: '251 and up', fee: 'Free', tone: 'free' },
];
---
<section id="tiers-20" class="st" aria-label="Subscription tiers">
  <div class="st-tiers">
    {view.map((t) => (
      <article class={`pt${t.featured ? ' pt--hot' : ''}`} data-tier={t.key}>
        <div class="pt__rail" aria-hidden="true"></div>

        <div class="pt__body">
          <div class="pt__top">
            <span class="pt__name">{t.name}</span>
          </div>

          {/* The three fields the selector drives. Each carries the opening value in the
              HTML so the card is complete before any script runs. */}
          <div class="pt__price">
            <div class="pt__priceRow">
              <span class="pt__was" data-was hidden={!t.open.was}>{t.open.was}</span>
              <span class="pt__amount" data-amount>{t.openPlan?.price}</span>
              <span class="pt__per" data-per>{t.openPlan?.per}</span>
            </div>
            <span class="pt__alt" data-alt>{t.open.alt}</span>
          </div>

          <div class="pt__billing">
            <span class="pt__billingLabel" id={`bill-${t.key}`}>Billing</span>
            <div class="pt__seg" role="group" aria-labelledby={`bill-${t.key}`}>
              {t.plans.map((p) => {
                const pl = plan(p.id);
                return (
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class={`pt__segBtn${p.id === t.sel ? ' is-on' : ''}`}
                    title={p.tip}
                    aria-pressed={p.id === t.sel ? 'true' : 'false'}
                    data-band
                    data-plan-id={p.id}
                    data-plan-url={pl?.url ?? ''}
                    data-amount={pl?.price}
                    data-per={pl?.per}
                    data-alt={p.alt}
                    data-was={p.was}
                  >{p.label}</button>
                );
              })}
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="pt__get">
            <span class="pt__summary">{t.summary}</span>
            <div class="pt__rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <ul class="pt__features">
              {t.features.map(([kind, text]) => (
                <li class={`pt__feat${kind === 'no' ? ' pt__feat--no' : ''}`}>
                  {/* THE GLYPH CARRIES THE SENSE. A tick beside "No rigging or skinning
                      tools" is what this replaces. */}
                  <span class="pt__glyph" aria-hidden="true">{kind === 'no' ? '×' : '✓'}</span>
                  <span class="pt__featText">{text}</span>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="pt__action">
          {t.mailto ? (
            <a class="pt__cta" href={t.mailto}>{t.cta}</a>
          ) : (
            <button
              type="button"
              class="pt__cta"
              data-buy
              data-plan-id={t.sel}
              data-plan-url={t.openPlan?.url ?? ''}
              disabled={!t.openPlan?.url}
            >{t.openPlan?.url ? t.cta : 'Coming soon'}</button>
          )}
          {t.footnote && <span class="pt__foot">{t.footnote}</span>}
        </div>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>

  {SHOW_SEAT_LADDER && (
  <div class="st-ent">
    <div class="st-ent__head">
      <span class="st-pill st-pill--ember"><span class="st-pill__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>ENTERPRISE</span>
      <p class="st-ent__line">All tools and priority email support, per named seat. Each band prices only the seats inside it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="st-table" role="table" aria-label="Enterprise per-seat price by seat count">
      <div class="st-row st-row--head" role="row">
        <span role="columnheader">SEATS</span>
        <span role="columnheader">PER SEAT / MONTH</span>
      </div>
      {BANDS.map((b) => (
        <div class={`st-row${b.tone ? ` st-row--${b.tone}` : ''}`} role="row">
          <span role="cell">{b.seats}</span>
          <span class={`st-row__fee${b.tone ? ` st-row__fee--${b.tone}` : ''}`} role="cell">{b.fee}</span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="st-callout">
      <svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 26 26" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 13h18M13 4v18" stroke="#FF7A3D" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" /></svg>
      <p>Past 250 seats, every seat is free. The whole studio tops out at <b>$3,125 a month</b>.</p>
    </div>
    {/* Enterprise is never a buy button: it is a "talk to us" mail link, always. */}
    <a class="st-ent__cta" href="mailto:adrian@fabricator.studio?subject=Enterprise%20pricing">Talk to us &rarr;</a>
  </div>
  )}

  {/* THE AUTO-RENEWAL DISCLOSURE. Not decoration and not a footer: US automatic-renewal
      law (ROSCA federally, and the state statutes California's ARL is the strictest of)
      wants the recurring terms and the cancellation route stated clearly BEFORE the
      charge, on the surface that takes it. Every button above starts a subscription that
      renews until it is cancelled, so the sentence belongs here rather than only inside
      the agreement it links to.

      RULED BY ADRIAN 2026-09-02. He was shown the sentence and said "Its fine", so it is
      no longer a placeholder. It is the shortest form that says the three things the law
      asks for: that it recurs, at what interval, and how to stop it. Those three facts do
      not come out. The phrasing is his to change and nobody else's. */}
  <p class="st-legal">
    Every plan is a subscription and <b>renews automatically until you cancel it</b>, weekly,
    monthly or yearly as shown. Cancel any time from your <a href="/account/">account</a>; you
    keep the period you have paid for. Sold by Stripe as merchant of record.
    <a href="/tools/eula/">Licence</a> &middot; <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>
  </p>

</section>

<script>
  // TWO JOBS, and they are separate on purpose.
  //
  // (1) THE BILLING SELECTOR. Pressing a band swaps the price, the per-unit, the alt line
  //     and the struck-through equivalent inside that card, and re-points that card's one
  //     CTA at the band now chosen. Purely local to the card; no other card moves.
  //
  // (2) THE CHECKOUT HANDOFF, unchanged in substance from the version this replaces. A
  //     visitor with no fs_session in localStorage can never reach checkout directly: a
  //     purchase made without a signed-in account cannot be attached to a seat, so a
  //     signed-out visitor goes to /account/ first. The destination is built AT CLICK TIME
  //     rather than at render, so a stale href never survives a sign-in that happens later
  //     on the same page load - and now, so it never survives a band change either.
  (function () {
    var API = 'https://api.fabricator.studio';
    var SESSION_KEY = 'fs_session';

    function getSession() {
      try { return localStorage.getItem(SESSION_KEY); } catch (e) { return null; }
    }

    // ---- (1) the selector -------------------------------------------------------------
    Array.prototype.forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll('.pt'), function (card) {
      var bands = card.querySelectorAll('[data-band]');
      var buy = card.querySelector('[data-buy]');
      var was = card.querySelector('[data-was]');
      var amount = card.querySelector('[data-amount]');
      var per = card.querySelector('[data-per]');
      var alt = card.querySelector('[data-alt]');
      if (!bands.length) return;

      Array.prototype.forEach.call(bands, function (b) {
        b.addEventListener('click', function () {
          Array.prototype.forEach.call(bands, function (o) {
            o.classList.toggle('is-on', o === b);
            o.setAttribute('aria-pressed', o === b ? 'true' : 'false');
          });
          if (amount) amount.textContent = b.getAttribute('data-amount') || '';
          if (per) per.textContent = b.getAttribute('data-per') || '';
          if (alt) alt.textContent = b.getAttribute('data-alt') || '';
          if (was) {
            var w = b.getAttribute('data-was') || '';
            was.textContent = w;
            // hidden, not display:none in CSS, so the row reflows with no empty gap.
            was.hidden = !w;
          }
          if (buy) {
            buy.setAttribute('data-plan-id', b.getAttribute('data-plan-id') || '');
            buy.setAttribute('data-plan-url', b.getAttribute('data-plan-url') || '');
            buy.disabled = !b.getAttribute('data-plan-url');
          }
        });
      });
    });

    // ---- (2) the checkout handoff -----------------------------------------------------
    var buys = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('[data-buy]'));
    if (!buys.length) return;

    // Resolved once and then read on every click, so a band changed after sign-in still
    // gets the right destination.
    var identity = null;

    function go(btn) {
      var url = btn.getAttribute('data-plan-url');
      if (!url) return;
      if (!identity) { window.location.href = '/account/'; return; }
      var params = [];
      if (identity.accountId) params.push('client_reference_id=' + encodeURIComponent(identity.accountId));
      if (identity.email) params.push('prefilled_email=' + encodeURIComponent(identity.email));
      window.location.href = url + (params.length ? (url.indexOf('?') === -1 ? '?' : '&') + params.join('&') : '');
    }

    buys.forEach(function (b) { b.addEventListener('click', function () { go(b); }); });

    var session = getSession();
    if (!session) return;

    fetch(API + '/v1/account', { headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + session } })
      .then(function (r) { return r.json(); })
      .then(function (data) {
        if (!data || !data.ok) return;
        // /v1/account returns `accountId`, confirmed against the live service. The
        // fallbacks stay because dropping client_reference_id is the right failure: the
        // service falls back to the address Stripe verified, which quietly does not work
        // when a buyer pays with a different address than they signed in with. Sending a
        // WRONG id would be worse than sending none.
        identity = {
          email: data.value.email || '',
          accountId: data.value.accountId || data.value.id || '',
        };
      })
      .catch(function () { identity = null; });
  })();
</script>

<style>

  .st-legal {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin: 2rem auto 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--bone-faint);
  }
  .st-legal b { color: var(--bone-dim); font-weight: 700; }
  .st-legal a { color: var(--bone-dim); }

  .st { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.75rem; }

  /* FOUR TIERS SINCE 2026-09-03, not three: Freelance Animator joined the row and the
     three-column grid left Enterprise orphaned on a line of its own. Four across on a wide
     screen, two-by-two in the middle band, one column on a phone (that last rule is further
     down and unchanged). PROVISIONAL LAYOUT, Adrian's to rule: two-by-two at every desktop
     width is the obvious alternative and is one line here. */
  .st-tiers { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; }
  @media (max-width: 1180px) {
    .st-tiers { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  }
  .st-pill {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem;
    border-radius: 9px;
    background: rgba(232, 224, 208, 0.06);
    border: 1px solid rgba(232, 224, 208, 0.25);
    color: var(--bone);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  }
  .st-pill__dot { width: 0.55rem; height: 0.55rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--bone-dim); }
  .st-pill--plasma { background: rgba(124, 255, 178, 0.13); border-color: rgba(124, 255, 178, 0.45); color: var(--bone); }
  .st-pill--plasma .st-pill__dot { background: var(--plasma); box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(124, 255, 178, 0.7); }
  .st-pill--ember { background: rgba(255, 122, 61, 0.13); border-color: rgba(255, 122, 61, 0.45); color: var(--bone); }
  .st-pill--ember .st-pill__dot { background: var(--ember); box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(255, 122, 61, 0.7); }

  .st-ent {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 22px;
    padding: 2rem 2.125rem 2.25rem;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--iron), var(--carbon));
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 122, 61, 0.35);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
  }
  .st-ent__head { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.9rem; align-items: flex-start; }
  .st-ent__line { margin: 0; max-width: 52rem; font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--bone-dim); }

  .st-table { display: flex; flex-direction: column; border: 1px solid var(--iron-3); border-radius: 14px; overflow: hidden; }
  .st-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; gap: 1rem; padding: 0.8rem 1.25rem; font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--bone-dim); border-top: 1px solid var(--iron-2); }
  .st-row--head { border-top: none; background: var(--iron); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.75rem; letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: var(--bone-faint); }
  .st-row__fee { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; color: var(--bone); }
  .st-row--free { background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(124, 255, 178, 0) 60%, rgba(124, 255, 178, 0.06)); }
  .st-row__fee--free { color: var(--bone); }

  .st-callout { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.85rem; font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--bone-dim); line-height: 1.5; }
  .st-callout svg { flex: none; }
  .st-callout p { margin: 0; }
  .st-callout b { color: var(--bone); }

  .st-ent__cta {
    align-self: flex-start;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--bone);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--iron-3);
  }
  .st-ent__cta:hover { border-color: var(--ember); }

  /* MOVED 900px -> 700px, 2026-09-03, and it was measured. 900 was set when these were
     three wide cards; the design's card is narrower and denser, so at 820px the single
     column stretched one card to 736px. 700 is also where Pro's 10px lift turns off, so
     the row becomes one column and flattens at the same width instead of two widths. */
  @media (max-width: 699px) {
    .st-tiers { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  /* ========================================================================================
     THE CARD, from his design drop. Values are the drop's, translated to this site's tokens
     wherever the drop used the token's own hex; the two that are not tokens are noted.
     ==================================================================================== */
  .pt {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    height: 100%;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-width: 0;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--iron);
    border: 1px solid var(--iron-2);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 34px rgba(11, 14, 16, 0.5);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  /* Pro sits 10px proud of the row. On one column the lift is dropped: with nothing beside
     it to be lifted ABOVE, it reads as a misaligned card instead of a featured one. */
  @media (min-width: 700px) {
    .pt--hot { transform: translateY(-10px); }
  }
